<BaseLayout title="Customer Success & Customer Operations" current="/customer-success/" description="Richard Allen's experience in customer success, customer experience, SaaS support, technical support, training, people leadership, retention, and customer operations.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Customer Success & Customer Operations</div><h1>Customer relationships backed by strong operating discipline.</h1><p class="lede">My customer-facing work combines relationship management, technical problem solving, training, escalation leadership, feedback loops, performance management, and the operational discipline needed to make service more consistent and scalable.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container grid two">
  <article class="card"><h2>HawkSoft management</h2><p>Progressed from Team Lead to Customer Support Manager in 2015 and managed 32 Customer Support and Technical Support representatives serving independent insurance agencies using HawkSoft software. I held hiring, firing, and disciplinary authority and managed workflow, attendance, escalations, quality, performance evaluations, coaching, and staff development.</p><p>I also worked directly with agency owners across the customer base, trained customers and staff on software features and workflows, and project-managed/coordinated database migrations between local networks and HawkSoft Online.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h2>Customer Journey & retention</h2><p>Co-led a cross-functional Customer Journey project for about a year, mapping touchpoints across an average customer relationship of roughly eight years—from initial need and sales through ongoing partnership and eventual retirement. The work materially helped improve customer retention by making friction, handoffs, and customer needs more visible across teams.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h2>Customer-service operations & OKRs</h2><p>Helped establish staff and departmental objectives and key results. Measures included calls taken, calls resolved, calls forwarded to Tier 2/3, call length, support tickets taken, tickets closed, and other service metrics. My team frequently exceeded peer teams on company OKRs.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h2>Reporting that changed operations</h2><p>Turned raw support and call data into recurring management reporting, analyzed trends, and recommended changes in staffing, training, policies, procedures, and future needs. My manager presented the reporting initially; I later presented most of it myself to directors and upper management, and the findings drove operational course corrections.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h2>Product & partner collaboration</h2><p>Regularly attended and contributed to Product Reviews and third-party partnership meetings, including presenting and at times leading discussions. This connected customer-support insight with development, product changes, partner relationships, and company leadership.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h2>The Kotter Group</h2><p>Established and managed a Customer Experience function and related operating processes. Maintained client relationships, gathered feedback, supported retention and service improvement, created training documentation and webinars, and later validated new software builds by checking intended functionality and whether changes disrupted existing features.</p></article>
</div></section>
